{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-names-plain-text","content":"# Extract names as plain text with json_xs\nUse when JSON stdin is an array of objects and the desired output is one name per line.\nRun with argv: [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-t\", \"string\", \"-e\", \"$_ = join \\\"\\\", map { \\\"$_->{name}\\\\n\\\" } @$_\"] and pass the JSON as stdin.\nThe Perl expression replaces the decoded array with a string; string output emits it without JSON quoting.\nVerify exit is 0, stderr is empty, and stdout contains each input name in order, one per line, with a final newline. Tested with Ann/30, Bob/25, Cy/41 and verified names only in order.\nDo not use --help (unsupported) or -t null (invalid format)."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
